    notes: [
        "Generated from maritime_route_mask_manual_v1.tif by tools/export_v0_authored_maritime_routes.py; do not hand-edit the points, only the id/stops if Matias corrects a route by hand.",
        "stops is Site(id) for a settlement within 700m of the traced junction, External(direction: North/South/East/West) for a route exiting the map canvas with no invented foreign port name, or Waypoint(x, y) for an unresolved open-water branch point the raster alone could not name -- see the module docstring stage 3 for how Waypoint stops arise; they are real graph branch points, not exporter failures, and are the ones most likely to need a future manual correction pass.",
        "Every route has exactly 2 stops (its two real/named/synthetic endpoints); multi-hop journeys through an intermediate settlement (e.g. Rios Port to Dromos City via Mazon Town) are exported as separate 2-stop route rows sharing the intermediate settlement id, not merged into one 3-stop row -- deliberate, so any one hop can be corrected without touching its neighbor.",
        "Itos Village and Nugget Field Mines are not covered by this mask (nearest paint 1.3-1.8km from either pin, outside the 700m snap radius) -- a separate land-connector problem, not this export.",
        "Traced segments whose start and end both resolve to the same place (a harbor commonly paints several short separate quay/approach spurs that each independently land within 700m of the same settlement pin) are dropped as local harbor-approach detail, not point-to-point trade routes; see the provenance JSON's route_summary.same_place_dropped for the count.",
